  "Bug_Title": "\"null\" should not be used with \"Optional\"",
  "Bug_Details": "Optional acts as a container object that may or may not contain a non-null value. It is introduced in Java 8 to help avoid NullPointerException . It provides methods to check if a value is present and retrieve the value if it is present.\nOptional is used instead of null values to make the code more readable and avoid potential errors.\nIt is a bad practice to use null with Optional because it is unclear whether a value is present or not, leading to\nconfusion and potential NullPointerException errors.",
